Subject: [PATCH] Mouse-resizable column band (drag the strip on the right of a column)

Column widths came only from [Column(weight)], compiled into the window class.
Rebalancing a band meant editing the attribute and waiting for a domain reload,
and the right split is a per-screen, per-session choice: the same window is used
docked narrow next to the Inspector and floating wide on a second monitor.

 - reserve a 5 px strip on the right of every band column and make it a
   splitter: drag moves width between the two slots it separates (their sum is
   preserved, so the rest of the band does not shift), double-click or
   right-click resets the tab to its authored weights;
 - a band has one slot more than it has columns, the trailing one being the
   empty space on the right of the last column: dragging the last strip sets how
   much of the window the band fills, instead of forcing it to span everything;
 - persist the resized band per window and per tab in EditorPrefs
   (Kontrols_<ns>_colw_<tab>, one CSV of weights), loaded lazily on first draw
   and written on mouse-up;
 - validate a stored layout against the live slot count, so adding or removing a
   [Column] in that tab drops the override instead of mis-applying it; a
   malformed or non-positive value is likewise ignored (a layout saved one value
   short is read as "no trailing space", which is how it used to render);
 - MinColumnWidth, protected virtual, 120 px: how narrow a column can be
   dragged. The trailing space has no floor and can close completely.

Narrow columns were the real floor, not the clamp: a control line is
[label 120][control][CC button 72][LFO handle 30], all fixed, so under roughly
300 px a line holding a slider stopped shrinking and overflowed into the next
column. The label and the CC button now scale with the column they sit in
(120 → 48, 72 → 36), and sliders carry an explicit 40 px minimum instead of
Unity's much larger default. A column wide enough for the authored sizes renders
exactly as before.

[Column(weight)] keeps authoring the default split and stays the layout you
ship. Public surface otherwise unchanged, no new attribute, and the strips are
taken out of the width the slots share rather than added to the band.

New file: Editor/KontrolsWindow.Layout.cs (partial KontrolsWindow).
Package: com.blindspot.kontrols 0.5.1 - Unity 6000.3.10f1
Rationale, decisions and known limits: see RAPPORT.md shipped alongside.
