 # Changelog
 
+## [Unreleased]
+
+### Added
+
+- **Mouse-resizable columns** — the 5 px strip on the right of a band column is
+  now a splitter. Dragging it moves width between the two slots it separates,
+  leaving the rest of the band untouched ; double-click or right-click it resets
+  the tab to its `[Column(weight)]` split. A band has one slot more than it has
+  columns : the last strip trades width between the last column and the empty
+  space on its right, so a band no longer has to fill the window. The layout is
+  persisted per window and per tab in `EditorPrefs`
+  (`Kontrols_<ns>_colw_<tab>`), and is dropped rather than mis-applied when the
+  number of `[Column]` in that tab changes. `[Column(weight)]` keeps authoring
+  the default split; no API change.
+- **`MinColumnWidth`** (`protected virtual`, 120 px) — how narrow a band column
+  can be dragged, overridable per window.
+
+### Changed
+
+- A control line now scales its two fixed-width parts with the column it sits
+  in : the side label (120 → 48 px) and the MIDI-Learn button (72 → 36 px), and
+  sliders carry an explicit 40 px minimum instead of Unity's much larger
+  default. A column wide enough for the authored sizes renders exactly as
+  before ; a narrow one stays readable instead of overflowing into its
+  neighbour.
+
